practice.prompt:
Summarize the paid orders in `orders.json`.

1. Print one compact line per order whose `status` is `paid`, as `{"id":...,"customer":...,"total":...}`, from the highest total to the lowest.
2. Then print one compact line `{"paid":N,"revenue":X}`: how many orders were paid, and the sum of their totals.

Expected output:

```text
{"id":5003,"customer":"Amina Diallo","total":506}
{"id":5015,"customer":"Amina Diallo","total":378}
{"id":5014,"customer":"Mei Lin","total":192}
{"id":5008,"customer":"Mei Lin","total":122}
{"id":5022,"customer":"Lucas Meyer","total":100}
{"id":5025,"customer":"Rita Gomes","total":58}
{"id":5024,"customer":"Mei Lin","total":31}
{"id":5011,"customer":"Sara Lindqvist","total":24}
{"id":5009,"customer":"Jon Eriksen","total":22}
{"id":5012,"customer":"Leila Karimi","total":20}
{"id":5018,"customer":"Amina Diallo","total":16}
{"id":5013,"customer":"Rita Gomes","total":9}
{"id":5021,"customer":"Ken Watanabe","total":8}
{"paid":13,"revenue":1486}
```

